WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.980
<b>Pork Foot Curry</b>

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.980
Chestnut Cookies

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:06.610
How was Takayama, Aoi-chan?

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:09.480
It was super cold, but I loved it.

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:15.490
We walked around Sanmachi and went to 
the snowy baths at Hirayu Hot Springs.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.650
Japanese-Western fusion snacks!

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.200
These chestnut cookie sandwiches are awesome!

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.500
Souvenir from Hida

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.500
<i>Souvenir from Hida.</i>

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:27.250
Chestnut cookies! Chestnut cookies!

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:24.850
How was Hamamatsu?

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:27.250
We chilled at Grandma's place.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:30.980
Rin-chan and my friend from back home
came over on the first day.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:35.010
My family came on the second day,
and we went for our New Year's shrine visit.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:37.370
Hamamatsu's got more to offer than just eel!

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.290
Turtle biscuits for the win!

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.770
Souvenir from Hamamatsu

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:40.770
<i>Souvenir from Hamamatsu.</i>

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:46.020
Turtle! Turtle! Turtle!

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:46.020
Rin-chan went camping by a beach in 
Iwata before coming to Hamamatsu.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.090
She sent me a ton of photos.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:52.280
The water was so pretty, wasn't it?

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:54.840
Packed with giant pig feet!

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.820
Iwata specialty, Pork Foot Curry!

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.530
Souvenir from Iwata

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:58.530
<i>Souvenir from Iwata.</i>

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:03.460
I'll eat that one at home...

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:05.310
Wise choice.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.510
Turtle Biscuits

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.510
Chestnut Cookies

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:43.260
<b>(2) Episode 4 
What Are You Buying With Your Temp Job Money?</b>

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:43.260
<b>(2) Episode 4 
What Are You Buying With Your Temp Job Money?</b>

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.010
A hexagon tarp!

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:43.260
<i>6,000 yen.</i>

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:44.710
Look what I bought!

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:47.300
Hey, you bought this one.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.270
Wow, a tarp!

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:54.720
After our Christmas camping trip, 
I figured we should have at least one.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:56.750
Tarp!

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.150
<b>Outdoor Activities Club</b>

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:03.780
Well, there's a lot going on, but since the 
Outclub is back, let's go set up the tarp.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.200
Sure.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:07.430
Tarp, tarp...

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:12.680
<i>And so they began setting up the tarp.</i>

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:19.850
<i>First, lay the tarp out on flat ground
that will easily take the pegs.</i>

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:23.930
<i>Next, extend the tarp poles.</i>

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:25.540
Oh.

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:27.520
I forgot the tarp poles at home.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.960
<b>End</b>

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:34.300
What?

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:36.300
We're screwed without the poles.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:37.150
Wait.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.440
Wait, wait, wait...

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:44.460
We can tie one side to a tree 
in place of a pole, and then...

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.620
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.730
Nadeshiko, you're the pole now!

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:50.320
What?!

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:59.090
<i>Attach the guy lines to the tarp 
and secure them with the pegs.</i>

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.470
<i>Erect the poles.</i>

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:08.220
<i>Finally, adjust the length 
of the guy lines for tension...</i>

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:12.260
<i>And you're done.</i>

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:14.140
Nice!

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.100
<i>To ensure that the tarp is stable,</i>

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:21.520
<i>make sure the guy lines, pegs, 
and poles are correctly angled.</i>

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.400
Just having a tarp really sets the mood, huh?

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.250
Right?

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:31.000
It really makes you feel like you're camping.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.850
<i>Tarps come in several materials:</i>

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:36.630
<i>nylon, which is highly portable,</i>

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:36.440
Nylon
Highly portable

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:40.630
Nylon
Highly portable

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:40.630
<i>and cotton, which is flame-retardant
so that campfires can be lit under it,</i>

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.630
Flame-retardant cotton
Campfires can be lit under it

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:42.320
<i>among others.</i>

00:04:52.510 --> 00:04:55.690
You know, that groundsheet Rin was using...

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:58.020
That would've been nice to have, too, huh?

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:00.730
I thought about that, too.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:07.230
It was a pain getting all that grass 
off the bottom of our tent.

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:12.540
And when we finally got it all off,
 there was grass on the top side.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:13.790
I know!

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:17.530
Rin-chan said we shouldn't need 
to spend more than 500 yen or so,

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:19.180
so let's buy one for next time.

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:20.480
Yeah.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:23.300
We'll have plenty of spending money 
from working all winter break, too.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.550
When are you getting paid, Nadeshiko-chan?

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:30.220
It's supposed to be deposited next week!

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:32.740
Are you finally gonna buy that lantern, then?

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:33.560
Yeah.

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:38.810
I couldn't wait, so I went back to 
Caribou the other day to stare at it.

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:41.010
What are you gonna buy, Aoi-chan?

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:42.410
I'm buying a chair.

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:45.180
A low chair like the one Rin-chan has.

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:46.820
Nice!

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:50.410
I want a hammock next.

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:52.070
A hammock!

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:54.010
I've seen them a lot on Namazon.

00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:56.830
The ones with the thick frames.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:00.490
Oh, yeah. Those are great,
since you can set them up anywhere.

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:03.590
You need a car to transport them
because they're so bulky, though.

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:06.450
So instead of a frame,
 I'll be using Nadeshiko and a tree.

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:09.450
That'll be 100 yen an hour!

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:11.100
That's dirt cheap.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:17.480
Also, we should find out if there's 
a cheaper way to get firewood.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:22.060
Even when it's 300 yen a bundle, 
you can burn through it pretty quick.

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:26.060
And when there's only the expensive stuff, 
you can't really use too much.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:32.180
You know, every time we have a 
campfire using firewood we paid for...

00:06:32.630 --> 00:06:37.230
I see those spinning billing meters they 
use for electricity and water and stuff.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:39.750
Y-Yeah, I guess I know what you mean.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:45.330
We still haven't had the heart to burn what 
we bought when we started the Outclub.

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:51.260
So that's why that firewood's 
been sitting there all this time.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:52.910
Come to think of it,

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:57.270
Eastwood Campgrounds was so awesome 
for letting us use all the wood we wanted.

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:59.090
I know, right?

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:04.820
Apparently they've started charging 
for firewood since the end of the year.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.200
They had a post on their blog about it.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:07.650
Wait, really?!

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:11.160
It must be because you made towers 
and burned them like crazy.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:11.160
Burn it all to the ground!

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:13.660
I-I never did such a thing!

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:16.670
They renovated the site, too. It's bigger now.

00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:17.910
Really?

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:24.360
Actually, there's a new camping place 
near Hottokeya Hot Springs now, too.

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:25.200
Seriously?

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:26.050
For real?

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:30.770
Apparently, there used to be a campground
 there a long time ago that shut down.

00:07:30.770 --> 00:07:34.400
They've set up a new one at the same place.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.650
Yeah?

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:38.360
We won't have to go far for the 
hot springs next time, then.

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:41.770
And we can buy fried hot spring
 eggs much more easily, Aki-chan.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:48.710
Lightly salted, crispy, creamy, 
fried hot spring eggs!

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:54.450
Add a dab of soy sauce, and have your 
fried hot spring eggs with rice!

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:59.450
Oh, no... I'm having flashbacks 
about the crispy creaminess...

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:03.250
Outclub tarp (some Nadeshiko required) 
currently under construction!

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:08.460
Those girls are such free spirits.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:13.840
Hey, have you two decided what you're 
buying with your temp job money?

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:16.900
You said you wanted a tent the other day.

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:18.060
Are you really buying one?

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:18.970
Yeah.

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:21.870
I actually ordered it already.

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:22.670
This one.

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.590
<i>The doggy tent.</i>

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:28.680
<i>Doubles as a dog house at home 
and on your camping trips.</i>

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:30.360
<i>10,000 yen, tax inclusive.</i>

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:32.650
This one's for dogs.

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:34.280
And it's pretty expensive...

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:38.130
I was looking for sleeping bags for 
dogs when I stumbled upon this.

00:08:38.130 --> 00:08:40.080
Before I knew it, it was in my cart.

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:43.150
But it's really elaborately made.

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:49.040
The poles attach with shock cords, 
making setup a breeze.

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:48.880
A dome tent with clip-on poles 
that comes with a fly sheet...

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:52.630
The fly sheet features ventilation 
holes that provide great breathability.

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:52.630
And the accessory poles make a tarp.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:58.160
<i>Wow, this thing is way better than some 
of the cheaper human tents out there.</i>

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:01.750
So what about a tent for you?

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:04.050
I can share with you guys for now.

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:05.320
Maybe next time.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:06.760
You crazy dog lady.

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:11.750
Wouldn't you love to see Chikuwa 
chilling in this tent, though?

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:17.240
Not really.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:18.720
<i>Holy crap, I wanna see that.</i>

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:22.390
The truth's written on your face, Rin.

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:30.550
So what are you going to buy, Rin?

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:34.040
There isn't really anything I want right now.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:35.890
I guess I'll save it for my next trip.

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:36.930
Yeah?

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:40.360
I wish I had, like, 100 million yen in savings.

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:42.100
Everyone does.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.980
What would you do with 100 million yen?

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:49.060
I guess I'd start by putting a sleeping 
bag on top and sleeping in it.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:52.070
Bye, Sensei.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:54.070
<b>Staff Office</b>

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:53.680
Bye.

00:09:55.750 --> 00:09:56.950
Good work, everyone.

00:09:57.220 --> 00:09:59.150
Good work!

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:03.450
Thank you!!
Please enjoy these snacks 
from Hamamatsu and Takayama!!

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:03.450
Turtle Biscuits

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:09.460
Thank you!!
Please enjoy these snacks 
from Hamamatsu and Takayama!!

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:18.840
Welcome.

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:26.670
Seki-san, Seki-san! 
The candle lamp girl's back.

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:28.230
So she is.

00:10:35.970 --> 00:10:38.660
She said she'd buy it once 
she got her paycheck.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:40.040
Do you think today's the day?

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:42.090
It's so adorable how gung-ho she is.

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:48.130
I remember shopping with 
my first paycheck as a student.

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:50.160
What did you buy?

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:52.240
I've forgotten now.

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:53.250
Oh, come on.

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:01.270
Should we set one aside for her?

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:02.560
Yeah.

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:09.300
<i>So cold...</i>

00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:14.340
<i>What should we make
 for our next camping trip?</i>

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:17.620
<i>We did Japanese food last time, so...</i>

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:19.530
<i>Maybe bread?</i>

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:33.350
<i>Maybe buttered, lightly browned muffins...</i>

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:39.420
<i>With bacon, lettuce, onions, 
and crushed boiled eggs,</i>

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:41.630
<i>tomato, and avocado 
sandwiched in between!</i>

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:46.370
<i>All with Caesar salad dressing!</i>

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:53.160
<i>And for soup, either minestrone 
or napa cabbage cream soup!</i>

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:30.970
<b>Minobu</b>

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:47.220
<i>The things you see, the things you eat...</i>

00:12:47.720 --> 00:12:50.350
<i>And you get to spend time 
contemplating things.</i>

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:56.880
<i>I think solo camping is a way 
to appreciate loneliness.</i>

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:02.070
<i>I love camping with everyone,</i>

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:08.950
<i>but I want to try solo 
camping like Rin-chan, too.</i>

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:19.560
<b>18 minutes from Kasugai Station</b>

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:19.560
<b>950 yen per hour (900 yen during training)</b>

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:19.560
Weekdays only! Well-loved by the locals!

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:20.940
This one's in Fuefuki.

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:23.240
<b>8 minutes from Sakaori Station</b>

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:23.240
<b>Starting at 980 yen per hour 
*Short-term/temp employment available</b>

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:23.240
Enjoy making houtou
Recommended for students and upstarts! 
Make some good cash during spring break! 

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:22.780
This one's in Kofu.

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:27.240
<b>Houtou Yosaku</b>

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:27.240
<b>Over 900 yen per hour!
 Extra for weekends and holidays</b>

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:27.240
Newly opening on March 1st!
 Looking for opening staff!
 Invite your friends to work with you!

00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:25.990
Hana-sushi?

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:27.240
This one's in Kofu, too.

00:13:30.290 --> 00:13:31.470
Kofu.

00:13:31.470 --> 00:13:32.700
This one's Kofu, too.

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:34.270
Kofu.

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:35.750
Kofu...

00:13:36.770 --> 00:13:41.750
<b>Near Minobu Station</b>

00:13:36.770 --> 00:13:41.750
<b>1,300 yen per hour
From 25,000 yen per month</b>

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:38.100
Minobu!

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:41.750
Seeking bus drivers!
 Two-day weekends / hiring bonuses
 Comprehensive training provided even for the inexperienced
 Up to 64 yrs. old; Class-2 Large Vehicle license required
 Uniform and commuter pass provided

00:13:39.990 --> 00:13:41.750
For a bus driver...

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:45.140
There's no work!

00:13:45.140 --> 00:13:50.000
Mom, isn't there anywhere around 
here that's hiring high schoolers?

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:51.700
Well...

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:55.200
Hagino nearby was just hiring part-timers,

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:57.390
but it seems they aren't anymore.

00:13:57.630 --> 00:13:58.910
Aw...

00:13:59.910 --> 00:14:03.950
Mom, is this the last of the pocket warmers?

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:05.590
They're gone already?

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:07.240
I'll buy some more later.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:10.370
Onee-chan, why do you use so 
many even though you drive?

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:12.410
My hands get cold when I'm outside.

00:14:12.770 --> 00:14:14.960
Your sister's sensitive to the cold.

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:20.290
By the way, you seem to be 
taking your time today.

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:24.800
It's already twenty past!

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:27.200
I'm gonna miss the train!

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:28.800
Have a good day!

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.680
I'm off!

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:35.860
Is she looking for a more long-term job?

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:38.310
Seems she's having a hard 
time finding one, though.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:44.830
There really isn't much around here.

00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:50.440
Your next job, huh?

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:54.200
It's so hard to find work.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:15:00.210
<b>Kofu

00:14:55.700 --> 00:15:00.210
<b>Kofu

00:14:56.030 --> 00:15:00.210
All the good jobs I see are in Kofu.

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:00.870
<b>Minobu</b>

00:15:01.180 --> 00:15:03.080
Found one in Minobu!

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:04.710
<b>Minobu</b>

00:15:03.660 --> 00:15:05.120
But then...

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:08.970
Shop Staff

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:08.970
It turns out that it's a full-time 
position or something.

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:15.800
Yeah, I saw an ad for a convenience store
 near my place at the end of the year,

00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:18.750
but it was gone two days later.

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:22.300
I wonder if there's a lot of competition 
because of the lack of job openings.

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:24.860
What kind of work are you 
looking for, Nadeshiko-chan?

00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:26.670
Let me think...

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:30.700
Anything would be fine, 
but preferably something fun.

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:32.860
A fun job, huh?

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:34.530
I know!

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:38.240
It would be seasonal, but wouldn't 
it be fun to work at a resort?

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:41.890
Oh, like a ski resort or a traditional inn?

00:15:41.890 --> 00:15:47.500
They were hiring live-in workers last 
summer at the campsite by Lake Yamanaka.

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:49.300
Working at a campsite?!

00:15:49.570 --> 00:15:54.310
Would that mean you get to camp 
every night after work?

00:15:54.310 --> 00:15:57.350
I don't know about that, 
but can you imagine?

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:01.920
Well, we'll let you know if either 
of our workplaces has an opening.

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:03.340
Thank you.

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:06.420
I borrowed the new issue 
of <i>Bivouac</i>. Wanna read it?

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:08.270
Yeah! I do!

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:10.780
<b>First-Time Winter Camping</b>

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:15.920
"Must-Haves for Winter Camping: Cozy Gear."

00:16:17.110 --> 00:16:20.850
Aoi-chan, are these like pocket warmers?

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:22.820
It's an oil heater.

00:16:22.820 --> 00:16:25.790
My grandma's always used one.

00:16:25.970 --> 00:16:30.810
You put oil inside and apply 
a lighter flame to the burner.

00:16:30.810 --> 00:16:35.300
You can reuse them, and they put out
 way more heat than the disposable kind.

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:37.140
That sounds awesome.

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:39.060
Isn't that dangerous, though?

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.950
You put oil in it and light it?

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:45.640
It's just the metal burner that 
reacts chemically and heats up.

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:47.740
There's no actual fire, apparently.

00:16:47.740 --> 00:16:49.320
Wow...

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:53.820
<i>A reusable hand warmer, huh?</i>

00:16:57.290 --> 00:16:58.540
Later, Nadeshiko.

00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:00.000
See you tomorrow.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.580
Yeah, see you!

00:17:08.140 --> 00:17:09.350
It's Onee-chan.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:14.090
I found a good tempura bowl shop 
near Minobu Station. Wanna come?

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:17.740
You're on your way home, aren't you?

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:20.600
<i>Minobu. Minobu.</i>

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:32.280
Found it! There it is!

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:36.530
I'm here, Onee-chan!

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:38.960
That was quick.

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:40.820
Two large shrimp tempura box sets, please.

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:42.040
Coming right up.

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:46.800
You don't invite me out 
for dinner very often.

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:48.620
I thought it'd be a nice change of pace.

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:51.040
Here you are.

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:54.050
With the heads!

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:54.050
Large Shrimp Tempura Box Set: 1,700 yen

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:56.060
Do I really deserve this?

00:17:56.060 --> 00:17:57.750
Was today a special day?

00:17:57.750 --> 00:17:59.550
Let's eat!

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:01.840
Yeah. It's your payday, isn't it?

00:18:01.840 --> 00:18:04.200
I thought you could treat me for once.

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:17.570
I-I-I was going to use the money to buy
a lantern and p-p-pay for camping and stuff!

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:18.820
I was kidding.

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:19.440
Huh?

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:21.940
You were looking for that, right?

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:26.080
<b>Now Hiring
 Part-Time Workers

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:24.820
Now hiring part-time workers...

00:18:24.820 --> 00:18:26.080
High school students welcome?!

00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:28.280
Are they looking for help here?!

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:30.080
That's what it says.

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:34.050
They've only just started hiring, so they 
haven't put ads in the job magazines yet.

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:47.100
Fujimoto

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:39.570
Yes! I'll do it! I'll do it!

00:18:39.570 --> 00:18:42.370
Pipe down. Your tempura bowl's getting cold.

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:54.610
<b>Subtotal</b>

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:54.610
<b>Running total</b>

00:18:57.340 --> 00:19:00.700
That'll be 7,370 yen for both.

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:02.870
Here's 10,000 yen.

00:19:04.050 --> 00:19:06.490
You finally bought it, Nadeshiko-chan.

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:07.120
Yeah!

00:19:07.260 --> 00:19:10.370
All right, Nadeshiko.
Let's take a commemorative photo.

00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:14.880
Look at her face!

00:19:15.180 --> 00:19:19.130
Please handle it carefully, 
as it's made with glass.

00:19:19.390 --> 00:19:21.120
Got it.

00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:42.750
Thank you.

00:19:43.460 --> 00:19:45.450
Thank goodness it didn't break.

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:48.550
The replacement chimneys for 
those are pretty expensive.

00:19:51.640 --> 00:19:52.590
All right.

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:55.740
You're one step closer to fancy camping.

00:19:55.740 --> 00:19:56.970
I know!

00:19:56.970 --> 00:20:00.040
Didn't you get something 
else, too, Nadeshiko-chan?

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:01.930
I caught a glimpse earlier.

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:04.930
That's a secret.

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:07.270
Why, though?

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:08.320
Tell us!

00:20:08.320 --> 00:20:10.380
It's a secret!

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:28.610
Really sets the atmosphere, doesn't it?

00:20:28.610 --> 00:20:31.230
It looks so nice and warm.

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:32.410
Right?

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:34.180
I'm home.

00:20:34.180 --> 00:20:35.620
Oh, welcome home.

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:42.160
You bought your lamp.

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:43.020
Yeah.

00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:44.930
I can't wait to use it on a camping trip.

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:48.930
Good for you.

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:49.910
Yeah.

00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:08.030
Thanks for all your help, Onee-chan!! 
Don't let the cold Yamanashi winter get you down!! 
-Nadeshiko

00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:08.030
<b>24 hours of warmth
Standard type</b>

00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:08.030
<b>Reusable</b>

00:23:12.280 --> 00:23:15.230
You said you were going to 
use the money for camping...

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:20.220
You didn't have to do this.

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:35.140
<b>Caribou-kun and Lake Yamanaka</b>

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:35.140
Next Episode

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:41.260
When camping...

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:41.260
Always mind the campsite 
and facility rules. Don't forget to 
take care of fires and your trash!

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:41.260
It gets cold during the winter. 
Stay warm and be well-prepared!

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:41.260
Outdoor Activities Club

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:41.260
<b>Ohohohoho</b>
